  "description": "Data import for WA.Core: reads flat files (Excel, CSV, JSON, XML, HTML, Markdown, DBF), maps their columns to a WA.FM table and converts every value to the target column type, reporting errors per row and column.",
  "id": "SI.WA.Import",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-09T13:39:56.597Z",
  "licenseFile": "LICENSE.txt",
  "licenseUrl": "https://aka.ms/deprecateLicenseUrl",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "ft0VsOntS/LkDInd1DXeOabfYmjCs4VDOgOIbzGzi/PsLNq5t+66CDskdz+o/+/FmjYattIU88smNIAc7tdEOA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 75838,
  "published": "2026-10-09T13:29:45.957Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0 -- First release: reading flat files (Excel .xls/.xlsx, CSV/TXT, JSON/JSON Lines, XML, HTML tables, Markdown tables, DBF), column mapping with automatic suggestions, conversion of every cell to the target column type with per-row errors before anything is written, and the writing into the target table (staging + one transaction, SQL Server and PostgreSQL, history in WA_ImportLog, the keys of the added rows in WA_ImportKeys). Templates (ImportTemplate): a saved import -- how to read the file, the target table, the mapping and the options -- applied to the next file of the same kind. An optional stored procedure run after the rows, in the same transaction. The data catalog (DataCatalog, tables WA_DataCatalog / WA_DataCatalogColumns from the database project): which roles may import into a table and which of its columns; TargetTable.KeyColumns keeps the key read back when a role may not import it. Requires SI.WA.DbRepository 2.2.0. No UI here (see WA.UI.Core for the import screen).",
